    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners` following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection convention.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Uses an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (matching the dedicated logger the tests capture).\n- Reads the persisted `@Val Owner` and logs an `info` line carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs after `SaveOwner` (when the id has been assigned) but on the successful-create path only. It's kept under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbours.\n\nBecause the id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` (a `LocalDate`) log via their natural `toString()` \u2014 which is the same ISO/text form the GET JSON exposes \u2014 the acceptance assertion that a single AUDIT line contains all three substrings passes.\n\nObserved log line during the test run:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-10\n```",
